From 978205e6a0f3716ab4838824ad1d0b2cd252f9fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cohost u2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 20:18:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Rest args on the caller's stack when they cannot escape;
 multimethod cache hit without the mutex; keyword dispatch inline

Draft: cohost doc/upstream/jank-25-variadic-multi.md.
Repro: bash dev/research/upstream/run.sh 25-variadic-multi (in johnmn3/cohost.cljc).

1. Variadic calls. At -Odirect-call (the -O3 default), the IR pass decides for a
   non-closure variadic fn whether the variadic arity's rest param can escape:
   it cannot when every reference to it is a direct argument of the inlined
   first, second, count or empty? (or it is unused), with only a whitelist of
   expression kinds in the body (a nested fn, letfn, try, def, raw C++ and
   the rest count as "can escape"). Such a fn carries rest_noescape_flag
   (bit 5 of its arity flags, unused before), and jit_variadic_function::call
   then passes the rest args as a native_array_sequence on the caller's stack
   (stack_rest_args, alive until the call returns) instead of a GC
   allocation. Escaping rest params keep the one allocation of 24.
2. Multimethods. reset_cache stored the hierarchy ref (the var) in
   cached_hierarchy while get_method compares it with hierarchy.deref() (the
   map), so the compare failed on every call: every call took the recursive
   mutex and reset the method cache, and find_and_cache_best_method handed
   the var to is_preferred, whose parents walk expects the map. It now stores
   hierarchy.deref() and passes the map to is_a (no longer dereffing) and
   is_preferred alike, as Clojure's MultiFn does. A keyword dispatch fn
   ((defmulti area :shape)) is computed inline as a get on the first
   argument; other dispatch fns and the method go through call_fast.

3. Lazily compiled fns (jank run's default). A deferred_cpp_function that is
   called through a captured value (a defmethod's method, a defmulti's
   dispatch fn, any fn held outside its var) took its recursive mutex on
   every call, compiled or not. realize() now returns on an atomic
   `realized` flag (set with release once compiled_fn is set), and call_fast
   calls a realized deferred fn's compiled fn directly (through its arity
   pointer when it is a jit_function).

The rest_noescape bit is computed in ir::arity_flags, so both the module
root fn (what def creates, lazily or eagerly) and nested fn expressions get
it.

